PART 4 -- THEOREM B: FIRST-STEP DIVISIBILITY, as a capacity test
 every path starts theta=e_1 from x=0 and reads m_h(0)=w, so omega(0,e_1) is a
 COMMON FACTOR of every W_T, hence omega(0,e_1) | c_alpha(t) in QQ[t].
   ribbon 2019  omega(0,e_1)=1        deg=0  divides c_alpha? True  (remainder 0)
   Psi 2011     omega(0,e_1)=1-t^w    deg=4  divides c_alpha? False  (remainder 3 - t**2)
   Gaussian     omega(0,e_1)=[w+1]_t  deg=4  divides c_alpha? False  (remainder 3 - t**2)
   deg_t c_alpha = 2 ; so any omega(0,e_1) of degree > 2 is DEAD by degree alone.
   integer form: omega(0,e_1)|_{t=1} must divide c_alpha(1)=2 in ZZ.
      Gaussian: [w+1]_t at t=1 = 5 ; 5 | 2 ? False

